<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>The Aspire Way — Soccer Fundamentals, Ages 6–8</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg?v=2" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <!-- generated-from: fa23c93 -->
    <div class="book">
      <!-- Cover -->
      <section class="book-cover">
        <div class="book-cover-kicker">Evidence-Based Youth Development Series</div>
        <h1 class="book-title">The Aspire Way</h1>
        <p class="book-cover-subtitle">Soccer Fundamentals, Ages 6–8<br />A Guide for Volunteer and New Coaches</p>
        <div class="book-cover-author">Aspire Sports</div>
      </section>

      <!-- Copyright page -->
      <section class="copyright-page">
        <p><strong>The Aspire Way: Soccer Fundamentals, Ages 6–8</strong></p>
        <p>Copyright © 2026 Aspire Sports. All rights reserved.</p>
        <p>
          No part of this publication may be reproduced, distributed, or transmitted in any form or by any means,
          including photocopying, recording, or other electronic or mechanical methods, without the prior written
          permission of the publisher, except in the case of brief quotations embodied in critical reviews and
          certain other noncommercial uses permitted by copyright law.
        </p>
        <p>Published by Aspire Sports · aspiresports.com</p>
        <p>First edition</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This guide is intended for educational purposes. Individual results vary; always
          use age-appropriate judgment and consult qualified coaching resources for your specific players.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Table of Contents -->
      <section class="toc-page">
        <h1>Contents</h1>
        <ul class="toc-list">
          <li><a href="#chapter-1">1. How Children Learn Soccer</a><span class="toc-dots"></span></li>
          <li><a href="#chapter-2">2. The Four Corners</a><span class="toc-dots"></span></li>
          <li><a href="#chapter-3">3. The Skills That Matter at 6–8</a><span class="toc-dots"></span></li>
          <li><a href="#chapter-4">4. Games, Not Drills</a><span class="toc-dots"></span></li>
          <li><a href="#chapter-5">5. Your First Sessions</a><span class="toc-dots"></span></li>
          <li><a href="#chapter-6">6. Talking to Parents</a><span class="toc-dots"></span></li>
          <li><a href="#back-matter">Skill Index</a><span class="toc-dots"></span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 1 -->
      <section class="chapter" id="chapter-1">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Chapter One</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">How Children Learn Soccer</h1>
        <p class="chapter-intro">
          Before a single drill or drawing of an activity, a coach needs a mental model of the player in front of
          them. A six-year-old is not a small adult. This chapter lays out how Aspire Sports thinks about the
          discovery and fundamentals stages of development, and the dozen principles that follow from that thinking.
        </p>

        <div class="domain-block">
          <h3>The Discovery Stage (Ages {discoveryStage.ageMin}–{discoveryStage.ageMax})</h3>
          <p>{discoveryStage.description}</p>
          <p><em>{discoveryStage.philosophy}</em></p>
          <ul>
            {discoveryStage.keyPrinciples?.map((kp) => <li>{kp}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Coach's role:</strong> {discoveryStage.coachRole}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="domain-block">
          <h3>The Fundamentals Stage (Ages {fundamentalsStage.ageMin}–{fundamentalsStage.ageMax})</h3>
          <p>{fundamentalsStage.description}</p>
          <p><em>{fundamentalsStage.philosophy}</em></p>
          <ul>
            {fundamentalsStage.keyPrinciples?.map((kp) => <li>{kp}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Coach's role:</strong> {fundamentalsStage.coachRole}</p>
          <p><strong>Practice-to-game ratio:</strong> {fundamentalsStage.practiceToGameRatio} · <strong>Max hours/week:</strong> {fundamentalsStage.maxHoursPerWeek}</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Twelve Principles Coaches Live By</h2>
        {principles.map((p) => (
          <div class="skill-block">
            <h3>{String(p.title)}</h3>
            <p>{String(p.principle)}</p>
            <p>{String(p.explanation)}</p>
            {Array.isArray(p.doExamples) && Array.isArray(p.dontExamples) && (
              <div class="coaching-tips">
                <h4>Do</h4>
                <ul>{(p.doExamples as string[]).map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}</ul>
              </div>
            )}
            {Array.isArray(p.dontExamples) && (
              <div class="common-mistakes">
                <h4>Don't</h4>
                <ul>{(p.dontExamples as string[]).map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}</ul>
              </div>
            )}
            {typeof p.europeanInsight === "string" && (
              <p><em>{p.europeanInsight}</em></p>
            )}
          </div>
        ))}
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 2 -->
      <section class="chapter" id="chapter-2">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Chapter Two</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The Four Corners</h1>
        <p class="chapter-intro">
          Aspire Sports organizes every player's development across four domains. No single one matters more than
          the others at this age — a confident, coordinated child who can't yet pass accurately is exactly where a
          six-year-old should be.
        </p>
        {domains.map((d) => (
          <div class="domain-block">
            <h3>{d.displayName}</h3>
            <p>{d.description}</p>
            <p><strong>Weight in overall assessment:</strong> {pct(d.weightInOverall)} · <strong>Assessed:</strong> {d.assessmentFrequency?.replace(/_/g, " ")}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 3 -->
      <section class="chapter" id="chapter-3">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Chapter Three</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The Skills That Matter at 6–8</h1>
        <p class="chapter-intro">
          These are the {soccerSkills.length} skills Aspire Sports tracks for the fundamentals stage, grouped by
          domain. Each includes a five-level progression so you can recognize where a player is now — not to sort
          players, but to know what to say next.
        </p>
        {domains.map((domain) => {
          const skillsInDomain = soccerSkills.filter((s) => s.domain === domain.name);
          if (skillsInDomain.length === 0) return null;
          return (
            <>
              <h2>{domain.displayName}</h2>
              {skillsInDomain.map((skill) => (
                <div class="skill-block" id={`skill-${skill.slug}`}>
                  <h3>{skill.name}</h3>
                  <div class="skill-meta">{domain.displayName}{skill.isCore ? " · Core Skill" : ""}</div>
                  {skill.description && <p>{skill.description}</p>}
                  {skill.progressionLevels && (
                    <table class="progression-table">
                      <tbody>
                        {([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] as const).map((level) => (
                          <tr>
                            <td class="level-num">{level}</td>
                            <td>{skill.progressionLevels![level]}</td>
                          </tr>
                        ))}
                      </tbody>
                    </table>
                  )}
                  {skill.coachingTips && skill.coachingTips.length > 0 && (
                    <div class="coaching-tips">
                      <h4>Coaching Prompts</h4>
                      <ul>{skill.coachingTips.slice(0, 4).map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}</ul>
                    </div>
                  )}
                  {skill.commonMistakes && skill.commonMistakes.length > 0 && (
                    <div class="common-mistakes">
                      <h4>Normal at This Age</h4>
                      <ul>{skill.commonMistakes.slice(0, 3).map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
                    </div>
                  )}
                </div>
              ))}
            </>
          );
        })}
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 4 -->
      <section class="chapter" id="chapter-4">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Chapter Four</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Games, Not Drills</h1>
        <p class="chapter-intro">
          Every one of these {soccerActivities.length} activities teaches a skill from Chapter Three through play,
          not repetition. Run them as written first; the variations exist for when your group needs more or less
          challenge.
        </p>
        {soccerActivities.map((activity) => (
          <div class="activity-card">
            <h3>{activity.name}</h3>
            <div class="activity-meta">
              {activity.difficulty} · {activity.minPlayers}{activity.maxPlayers ? `–${activity.maxPlayers}` : "+"} players · {activity.durationMinutes} min
              {activity.spaceRequired ? ` · ${activity.spaceRequired} space` : ""}
            </div>
            {activity.description && <p>{activity.description}</p>}
            {activity.skillsDeveloped && activity.skillsDeveloped.length > 0 && (
              <p>
                <strong>Builds:</strong>{" "}
                {activity.skillsDeveloped.map((slug) => skillNameBySlug.get(slug) ?? slug).join(", ")}
              </p>
            )}
            {playSummary(activity) !== activity.description && <p>{playSummary(activity)}</p>}
            {activity.equipmentNeeded && activity.equipmentNeeded.length > 0 && (
              <p><strong>Equipment:</strong> {activity.equipmentNeeded.join(", ")}</p>
            )}
            {activity.coachingPoints && activity.coachingPoints.length > 0 && (
              <div class="coaching-tips">
                <h4>Coaching Points</h4>
                <ul>{activity.coachingPoints.slice(0, 5).map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}</ul>
              </div>
            )}
            {activity.commonMistakes && activity.commonMistakes.length > 0 && (
              <div class="common-mistakes">
                <h4>Common Mistakes</h4>
                <ul>{activity.commonMistakes.slice(0, 4).map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
              </div>
            )}
            {activity.variations && activity.variations.length > 0 && (
              <p>
                <strong>Variations:</strong>{" "}
                {activity.variations.map((v) => `${v.name} (${v.description})`).join("; ")}
              </p>
            )}
            {activity.makeEasier && (
              <div class="make-easier-harder">
                <h4>Make It Easier</h4>
                <Fragment set:html={bulletBlockToHtml(activity.makeEasier)} />
              </div>
            )}
            {activity.makeHarder && (
              <div class="make-easier-harder">
                <h4>Make It Harder</h4>
                <Fragment set:html={bulletBlockToHtml(activity.makeHarder)} />
              </div>
            )}
          </div>
        ))}
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 5 -->
      <section class="chapter" id="chapter-5">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Chapter Five</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Your First Sessions</h1>
        <p class="chapter-intro">
          {soccerSessionPlans.length} ready-to-run session plans for the fundamentals stage, in the order you'll
          likely need them: an opening day, ball-mastery basics, dribbling, passing, and a pre-game warmup. Each
          segment lists what to run and why — adapt the timing to your group size and attention span.
        </p>
        {soccerSessionPlans.map((plan) => (
          <div class="session-plan">
            <h3>{plan.name}</h3>
            <div class="activity-meta">{plan.durationMinutes} minutes total</div>
            {plan.description && <p>{plan.description}</p>}
            {plan.equipmentNeeded && plan.equipmentNeeded.length > 0 && (
              <p><strong>Equipment:</strong> {plan.equipmentNeeded.join(", ")}</p>
            )}
            <div class="session-plan-structure">
              {plan.structure.map((segment) => (
                <div class="session-segment">
                  <h4>{segment.name} <span class="skill-meta">— {segment.type} · {segment.durationMinutes} min</span></h4>
                  {segment.description && <p>{segment.description}</p>}
                  {segment.activitySuggestions && segment.activitySuggestions.length > 0 && (
                    <p><strong>Try:</strong> {segment.activitySuggestions.join(", ")}</p>
                  )}
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
            {/* A few plans carry `coachingNotes` as a short pull-quote; others
                duplicate the entire session as one markdown-formatted
                narrative (6,000+ chars, headers/checkboxes/bold included) —
                already covered by the structure segments above, so skip the
                long form rather than dumping raw markdown syntax onto the page. */}
            {plan.coachingNotes && plan.coachingNotes.length < 700 && (
              <p><em>{plan.coachingNotes}</em></p>
            )}
          </div>
        ))}
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 6 -->
      <section class="chapter" id="chapter-6">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Chapter Six</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Talking to Parents</h1>
        <p class="chapter-intro">
          A coach who can explain "why" to a parent — why there's no scoreboard, why every child plays every
          position, why practice looks like games instead of lines and drills — earns the trust that makes the rest
          of this book possible.
        </p>
        <div class="skill-block">
          <h3>From Discovery to Fundamentals</h3>
          <p>
            Most parents joining a fundamentals-stage ({fundamentalsStage.ageMin}–{fundamentalsStage.ageMax}) team
            remember discovery-stage ({discoveryStage.ageMin}–{discoveryStage.ageMax}) soccer as pure play — no
            positions, no plan, everyone chasing the ball. That instinct doesn't disappear at six; it gets
            channeled. The fundamentals stage keeps discovery's core promise (fun first, everyone touching the ball
            constantly) while layering in the ABCs — agility, balance, coordination, speed — through the same games
            format, never through lines or lectures. Parents who understand that continuity stop asking "when do we
            start real practice" and start noticing their child's balance, first touch, and confidence improving
            every week.
          </p>
        </div>
        {parentResources.map((resource) => (
          <div class="skill-block">
            <h3>{String(resource.title)}</h3>
            {typeof resource.description === "string" && <p><em>{resource.description}</em></p>}
            <Fragment set:html={markdownToHtml(String(resource.content))} />
          </div>
        ))}
      </section>

      <!-- Back matter: skill index -->
      <section class="chapter" id="back-matter">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Index</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Skill Index</h1>
        <ul class="back-matter-index">
          {[...soccerSkills]
            .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))
            .map((skill) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`#skill-${skill.slug}`}>{skill.name}</a>
              </li>
            ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <script>
      import { Previewer } from "pagedjs";

      const previewer = new Previewer();
      previewer
        .preview(undefined, undefined, document.body)
        .then((flow: { total: number }) => {
          (window as any).__pagedPageCount = flow.total;
          (window as any).__pagedDone = true;
        })
        .catch((err: unknown) => {
          console.error("paged.js preview failed", err);
          (window as any).__pagedError = String(err);
          (window as any).__pagedDone = true;
        });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
